# The sim can put the aeroplane somewhere the state machine cannot reach on its
# own: teleport to a gate from the map, "start a flight here", a repaired crash.
# Without the resync the announcer sits in the cruise forever and says nothing
# for the rest of the session.
#
# The 20 second wait matters as much as the reset: a momentary touchdown must
# not be mistaken for a teleport to the stand.

library BoardingStarted BoardingWelcome

# The power is switched on for a moment and off again, rather than simply left
# at zero. Left at zero it reads as Unknown - "this aeroplane publishes no such
# switch" - and then the cabin opens without waiting for power, which is the
# right answer for a FlightFactor and the wrong test for a teleport. Only a
# dataref that has been seen to move counts as a switch somebody drives, and
# the 1.x side of the differential reads real datarefs, so the movement has to
# happen in the scenario. See 14-blind-aircraft.scn for the other half of the
# rule. None of this is visible in the air: the aeroplane starts in the cruise.
set hour=9 seatbelt=0 battery=1 nav=1 taxi=1
set on_ground=0 agl_ft=34000 alt_ft=35000 vs_fpm=0 gs_kt=450 engines=2
advance 10
set battery=0 nav=0 taxi=0 logo=0
advance 20
expect phase CRUISE

# Teleported to a stand: on the ground, engines off, stationary.
set on_ground=1 agl_ft=0 alt_ft=100 gs_kt=0 engines=0
advance 15
expect phase CRUISE          # still inside the 20 s grace period

advance 20
expect phase PREFLIGHT

# And from there the normal ground logic takes over again.
set battery=1 nav=1
advance 10
expect phase BOARDING
expect played BoardingStarted
